      "summary": ": Rātū/Tuesday The grooming and snowmaking teams have been working hard all night, and so has the wind! There's some enjoyable cord to kick things off in Home Basin. And there will be some wind blown deposits of chalky snow and fun drifts to play on. That wind will have stripped quite a few places, so caution required. Cold temperatures are on the menu, so rug up warm today. We will start with Home Basin and delayed in the Saddle while the wind eases and we assess the terrain, but we do expect to get that open later today, all going well. The coffee machine is fired up and the scones are in the oven. Please can everyone respect the slow zone on Triple Treat. This is a space for learners to take time and flying past people at speed is scary and risks collision. -- Home Basin- Open Saddle Basin- Open Matukituki Basin- Open Summit Slopes- Open Motatapu Chutes- Closed Sundance- Closed Backcountry Access- Delayed Skinning Access- Open Beginner Platter- Open",
